From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Let an uncached picture's image go once it is a texture

An Image read with cache: false is read for that Image alone, yet its
texture factory kept the file's pixels for as long as it was shown,
beside the texture made of them: a full-screen wallpaper of 2880 by
1800 pixels held 20 MB of memory it never read again. Once such a
picture's factory has made a texture it now lets the image go, keeping
only how it was read, and reads the file again, as it was, for another
texture or anyone asking for the image, as when a window is made again
for another screen. QSG_TRANSIENT_IMAGES lets every image go, and a
cached picture shown in a second window then draws nothing, so only an
uncached picture from a local file read by Qt's own reader lets go.

---
--- a/src/quick/util/qquickpixmap_p.h
+++ b/src/quick/util/qquickpixmap_p.h
@@ -39,11 +39,21 @@
     QSGTexture *createTexture(QQuickWindow *window) const override;
     QSize textureSize() const override { return size; }
     int textureByteCount() const override { return size.width() * size.height() * 4; }
-    QImage image() const override { return im; }
+    QImage image() const override;
+
+    // Lets go of the image once a texture is made of it, for a picture read
+    // uncached from a file, which nothing else shares: the texture holds it,
+    // and the file is read again, as it was, should another be asked for.
+    void letGo(const QUrl &url, const QRect &region, const QSize &requested,
+               const QQuickImageProviderOptions &options, int frame, qreal ratio);
 
 private:
+    struct Reading;
+    QImage readAgain() const;
+
     QImage im;
     QSize size;
+    std::shared_ptr<const Reading> reading;
 };
 
